  {
    "request_id": "53809b841d4f",
    "user_id": "customer-6",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-19T13:04:25.198615+00:00",
    "input": "Can I withdraw cash from an ATM abroad with my debit card?",
    "input_sha256": "d4fd72fd3487e6b70a2335086efbe826c2d283f85a6b4b71ed0346a4d06be72f",
    "input_chars": 58,
    "output": "Yes, you can generally withdraw cash at ATMs abroad **if** VinBank’s cards are accepted in that location and your debit card meets the requirements there. However, this depends on:\n\n- **VinBank’s presence** in the country – some regions may only support US-based debit cards or require local cards.\n- **Your card type** – certain debit cards may be restricted for international use.\n- **ATM operator** – the machine itself must accept your card.\n\nTo proceed safely:\n1. Verify that your debit card is enabled for international transactions in the destination country.\n2. Check if the local ATM network supports VinBank cards; sometimes you’ll need to use a partnered network or a local branch.\n3. Ensure you have enough available balance before traveling.\n\nIf you’re unsure about availability in a specific country, contact your local VinBank branch or check our website’s “Travel & International Use” section. Let me know if you’d like help finding the nearest branch or understanding any related fees!",
    "blocked": false,
    "layer": null,
    "latency_ms": 2656.2,
    "completed_at": "2026-11-19T13:04:27.860044+00:00"
  },
